  "term": "long-term potentiation",
  "definition": "Long-term potentiation is a lasting strengthening of how effectively one nerve cell signals another at a synapse, usually after those same connections have been activated in a suitable way. Its features suggest it may be one of the cellular processes involved in learning and memory.",
